  - m_Id: 1049440586186752
    m_Localized: 'Vas deferens: Conducts sperm from the epididymis into the abdominal
      cavity, combines with the secretory duct of the seminal vesicle to empty into
      the urethra.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1049660652929024
    m_Localized: 'Scrotum: Dark skin sac containing the testicles, which is elastic
      for thermoregulation.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1049793264238592
    m_Localized: 'Penis: Composed of erectile organs: 2 corpora cavernosa (located
      above) and 1 spongy body (located below, containing the urethra).'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1049887090819072
    m_Localized: 'Seminal vesicles: Located behind the bladder, in front of the rectum.
      Secrete the nutritional components of semen.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1049904413294592
    m_Localized: 'Prostate: Located below the bladder, surrounding the urethra. Secretes
      alkaline fluid to neutralize vaginal acid.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1050388020740096
    m_Localized: 'Fallopian tube: Structure: Ovarian tube from the ovary to the uterus.
      Segments: 4 segments (Funnel, Ampulla, Isthmus, Wall). Note: Fertilization
      usually occurs in the outer 1/3 (ampulla).'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1050388754743296
    m_Localized: 'Ovaries: Location: Located against the side wall of the pelvis
      (in the ovarian fossa). Function: Creates ova (eggs) and secretes female hormones
      (Estrogen, Progesterone). Shape: Flat bean-shaped.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
